      "message": "Could the message describe what this changes on top of its parent? As far as I can see, the proposed slice is already carried: `VMG_MMAP_STATE()` and `VMG_VMA_STATE()` set `vmg-\u003eslice_off`, and aosp/4367981 sets it in `copy_vma()`. B10 also already compares slices on both sides for files with `vm_ops`.\n\nWhat\u0027s missing is the case of `vm_file` without `vm_ops` (private /dev/zero and private ashmem). Their prev check skipped the slice, so an `mprotect()`, `madvise()` or `mremap()` merge could leave existing pages at the wrong slice. Their faults are anonymous, so I don\u0027t think \u0027faults the wrong file bytes\u0027 applies. Once the code settles, something like this, with a body that says what fails without it:\n\n```\nANDROID: P3S: mm: vma: Compare slices of private /dev/zero merges\n```",
